+### (c) SG11 correctness fix: **KEEP** (commit `51098e0`) (2026-06-17)
+
+**GATE-BLIND CORRECTNESS BUG — found by the 30-agent megakernel bug-hunt (`.perf/megakernel_bug_hunt.json`).**
+
+The L3-TC staged SuperGrok11 gate in `opt_stages_precompute.cuh` computed
+`cos(grad, MU)` (the SharpnessMetaNet output, a scaled/clipped momentum) instead of the canonical
+`cos(grad, MOMENTUM)` (the raw Adam `exp_avg`) in all 3 SG11 megakernel cells
+(decoder/vit/mamba). The gate is `sigmoid(gate_temp * cos_sim)` and scales the entire
+`(1-gate) * alpha * mu` smart-gradient term every step — so every SG11 training trajectory since the
+staged path was introduced was using the wrong algorithm.
+
+**Why it was GATE-BLIND (both conditions had to co-occur):**
+1. **Co-wrong oracle:** the fp64 oracle in `test_opt_stages.py` and `test_l3tc_tail_gate.py` was written
+   to mirror the kernel formula (computing `cos(grad, mu)`) rather than the canonical algorithm. Kernel
+   == oracle → parity always passed. This is the classical "test-the-implementation-not-the-spec" trap.
+2. **Step-1 coincidence:** at step 1 the SharpnessMetaNet `rescale=0` makes `mu ≈ 0` AND `exp_avg=0`,
+   so `den_m ≈ 0 → cos = 0 → gate = sigmoid(0) = 0.5` in BOTH formulations. The single-step fp64 gate
+   is incapable of distinguishing `cos(grad, mu)` from `cos(grad, momentum)` at step 1.
+   Divergence only appears once `rescale ≠ 0` and momentum accumulates (many training steps in, at scale).
+
+**Fix:** routed the staged Sweep-A reduction through canonical `algo::sg11_sweep_a_step` (the single
+source that accumulates over `momentum` and writes `mu` in one pass) + `sg11_finalize_gate`. Call sites
+now pass `st.exp_avg` (the start-of-step momentum, captured before `sg11_sweep_b_step` writes it).
+Removed the now-unneeded `__syncthreads`. De-mirrored the oracles (both test files now encode
+`cos(grad, momentum)` from first principles). Extended `check_math_single_source.py` with a
+cosine-reinline scan on `opt_stages_precompute.cuh` + `#include` assert.
+
+**Gate (parity-BREAKING, intentional — corrected operand):**
+- OLD kernel FAILS warm-up gate (gate diff 0.74–0.92 vs momentum reference).
+- NEW kernel PASSES all 3 SG11 cells × 3 seeds (diff ≤ 8.6e-3 vs momentum; ~100× separation from mu).
+- Full 33-cell gate GREEN × 3 seeds (no regression to non-SG11 cells).
+- A/A/A bit-identical.
+- Gated with a WARM-UP step (nonzero `exp_avg`) to defeat the step-1 coincidence.
+
+**Drift-audit result:** the 23-agent `optimizer_drift_audit.json` audit of all 11 optimizers'
+L3-TC staged paths confirms SG11 was the only optimizer with this class of drift. The fix is now
+canonical; no other optimizer carries an active SG11-class wrong-operand divergence.
+
+**Follow-up (load-bearing, NOT yet done):** `run_sg11_warmup_gate` is CLI-only. Wire it into a
+pytest-collected hw test (oracle-trust-audit queue item) so the cos-operand class is
+CI-regression-guarded. Without this, a future regression to `cos(grad, mu)` would again be gate-blind.
+
